ADR-0039 ruling 4: the Edge.quality {score, reason} block carried zero
independent signal — quality.score was round(clamp(confidence), 3) (110,533/
110,533 corpus edges) and quality.reason encoded the emitter mechanism, not a
confidence tier. The one-version deprecation window (opened at schema 0.14.6)
has elapsed; the human flagged removal ready.

Removed: the Edge.quality field, its __post_init__ auto-derivation, the
_derive_edge_quality() helper, and the to_dict/from_dict wiring. Edge.from_dict
still tolerates a legacy "quality" key on pre-0.20.0 cached artifacts (ignored,
not resurrected). The stale "quality" schema decoration in generate_schema_lib
is removed and docs/schema.json regenerated.

SCHEMA_VERSION 0.19.0 -> 0.20.0 (breaking output-format change). Consumers read
confidence + confidence_source + is_resolved (and rank_score for ranking)
instead — no src code outside ir.py read edge.quality. Spec §12/§9 updated.

The unrelated Symbol.quality (Node-level, INV-nuzal declared-but-empty) is
untouched.

Closes WI-riguh + WI-humok (G4 / ADR-0039 confidence tail).

